    "encompassment_scope": [
      "Encompassment applies only when the broader class the ordinance regulates is electric transmission itself or electric lines/facilities that logically include high-voltage transmission: extract when the provision governs 'electric transmission', 'electric transmission lines', 'electric lines', 'electric utility lines', or 'electric facilities' without a voltage qualifier and does not carve out transmission or limit itself to lower-voltage/distribution infrastructure. All electric transmission — and unqualified electric-line or electric-facility language — includes high-voltage transmission, so such wording is in scope.",
      "Electric anchors also include electric substations (for example 'public utility substations', 'electric substation', 'switchyard') and the physical plant of a named electric utility described as a 'light', 'power', or 'electric' company — its 'poles, towers, wires, cables, conduits' or similar equipment. When such electric items appear in a provision that also lists non-electric utilities (telephone, telegraph, gas, pipeline, water, sewer, railroad, cable), the provision remains in scope for the electric portion: extract only the electric items, quote them verbatim, and ignore the non-electric ones.",
      "Do NOT apply encompassment to generic wording that does not name electric transmission or electric lines/facilities. In particular, 'all development', 'all construction', 'all subdivision improvements', 'any floodplain development', 'all public utilities', 'all utilities', 'all utility infrastructure', and 'any work within public streets or rights-of-way' do not by themselves include high-voltage electric transmission — a bare 'utility' or 'development' class does not entail transmission. Require electric-transmission or electric-line/electric-facility wording before extracting by encompassment.",
      "Do not apply encompassment to provisions explicitly scoped to a non-transmission technology (for example 'water systems only', 'gas pipelines only', 'wind energy conversion systems only'); those remain out of scope.",
      "Do not apply encompassment to provisions explicitly scoped to lower-voltage electric infrastructure only (for example 'distribution lines', 'service drops', 'secondary lines', 'sub-transmission lines', or clauses bounded by a voltage cap below the ordinance's own transmission-line threshold). When the ordinance defines 'transmission line' by a minimum voltage, treat provisions restricted to voltages at or below that threshold as out of scope. A generic reference to 'distributing equipment' or 'distribution' used loosely to describe a light/power company's equipment does not by itself invoke this exclusion; apply the exclusion only when the provision is explicitly and exclusively limited to distribution, service, secondary, or sub-transmission voltages (for example by a stated voltage cap, or by scoping the whole provision to distribution lines).",
